{
  "schema": "durable-workflow.server-parity-fixture/v1",
  "id": "child-retries",
  "review_state": "reviewed",
  "contract": "A child's retry and timeout options (published Server 2.11.7 with Workflow 2.15.7 ChildWorkflowRetryPolicy and the bridge's startChildRetryIfAvailable), over raw worker HTTP on protocol 1.20 in a fresh namespace. Each case starts a parent with one start_child_workflow command carrying retry_policy, execution_timeout_seconds or run_timeout_seconds, then fails, completes or late-completes the child's runs. The call, ChildWorkflowScheduled, ChildRunStarted and the child's WorkflowStarted record a retry snapshot and a timeout snapshot; a policy with no known key records nothing. A failed or timed-out child run is retried as a new run of the same child instance under a new link while the policy has attempts left and the failure is retryable; the retry keeps the call and the execution deadline, takes a new run deadline, and waits out the backoff, and the parent stays waiting for the child. A failure marked non-retryable or of a type the policy names, or the last attempt's failure, fails the parent's call. IDs are labels in order of first appearance and deadlines are recorded by presence. Embedded applications have no worker protocol.",
  "workflow_type": "parity.v1.echo",
